                <pb facs="1234" n="1084" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1084"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 8684/3.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Swedish
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-10-12"><hi rendition="#italic">October 12,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 36.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the department’s note of the
                    4th instant in regard to the proposed increase of taxes in Cairo with a view to
                    the construction of a sewer system, I have the honor to say that the agent of
                    the United States at Cairo having reported that American interests will be
                    slightly, if at all, affected by the proposed increase of the tax on rental
                    valuation of realty, he has been instructed that he may assent thereto, if the
                    assent of the United States be necessary to insure unanimity.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
